om 1901 until the German Revolution.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-ewart-gladstone"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-ewart-gladstone.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William Ewart Gladstone</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William Ewart Gladstone was a British Liberal statesman who served four times as prime minister between 1868 and 1894.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-fiennes-1st-viscount-saye-and-sele"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-fiennes-1st-viscount-saye-and-sele.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William Fiennes, 1st Viscount Saye and Sele</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William Fiennes, 1st Viscount Saye and Sele, was an English nobleman and Puritan leader who opposed Charles I's prerogative taxation.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-fitzosbern"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-fitzosbern.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William FitzOsbern</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William FitzOsbern was a Norman lord, kinsman and close adviser of William the Conqueror, and one of the planners of the invasion of England in 1066.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/william-fitzwilliam-owen"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/william-fitzwilliam-owen.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">William Fitzwilliam Owen</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">William Fitzwilliam Owen was a British naval officer and hydrographer who surveyed much of the coast of East and West Africa in the 1820s.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-